[Readout]
  Class counts here use full directed tournament isomorphism over [0,1).
  Folded, complement-merged, or endpoint-inclusive conventions may count differently.
  Tight rows keep the marked node at 1/14.
  Divisibility failures migrate upward to q(S)<14.
  Farey-neighbor failures migrate downward to p/q with q-14p=-1.
  The spectrum walk confirms the metagraph hook: phase breakpoints are arc-flip events,
  generically single flips and at symmetric phases multi-flips.
